Pin exit-status propagation of the real gates invoked by the package suite.

Decision and reason:
- check-nsis-migration.test.ps1 invokes the production syntax gate and the production validator with the call operator. Today every failure path in that chain is a thrown error (verified: no exit and no Write-Error in check-nsis-migration.ps1, its dot-sourced modules, or test-install-ps1.ps1), so failures propagate under ErrorActionPreference=Stop.
- That guarantee rested only on the throw-only property staying true. If a future failure path used an exit code instead, the suite would silently stay green. Assert-True $? after each of the two invocations pins the guarantee permanently.
- Both invocations are pinned, not just the validator: leaving one unpinned would be a half-adopted mechanism.

Scope:
- scripts/release/check-nsis-migration.test.ps1 only, +2 lines. No production code changed.

